    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφιππος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unsuited for cavalry,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					3.4.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				47
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>unused to riding,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππικός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.Socr.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1608
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1.15
			</span></i>; <i>ignorant of horsemanship,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				350a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				335c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nav.</u>
				30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>without cavalry,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				4.6.6
			</span></i>.</div>
